       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose needs to be checked first.\n\n**The problem:** Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is 5 times the usual adult maximum of 200 mg/day. Adults usually start at 25\u201350 mg once daily and increase as needed, staying within 50\u2013200 mg/day. A 1000 mg daily dose is in overdose range and carries a risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation and seizures.\n\nThis looks like it could be a typo, maybe an extra zero for **100 mg**.\n\n**Please confirm the dose you want:**\n- **100 mg by mouth once daily** (if 1000 was a typo)\n- **50 mg by mouth once daily** (a common starting dose)\n- Or another dose within 25\u2013200 mg/day\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away. If you really do mean a dose above 200 mg/day, please tell me the clinical reason so I can add it to the order note. Even then, I'd strongly recommend checking with pharmacy first."
